  "blog_dividends_pay_date": "Pay date",
  "blog_dividends_paragraph_one": "Apple's forward dividend yield currently stands at 0.47%, down from its 5-year average of 0.72%. This is a significant decline of about 34.71% from the historical norm, so investors may be receiving less income than in previous years. Even so, Apple recently increased its dividends per share by about 4.17%.",
  "blog_dividends_paragraph_two": "Over the longer term, Apple's dividends per share have grown at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of about 5.37% over the past five years, showing consistent dividend growth. Apple's payout ratio and free-cash-flow payout ratio are also favorable at about 14.87% and 14.65%. These ratios show that Apple uses only a small share of earnings and free cash flow for dividends, leaving room for future increases or other shareholder-friendly uses without straining its finances.",
  "blog_dividends_paragraph_three": "In summary, Apple's current dividend yield is below its five-year average, but the company still shows solid fundamentals through rising dividends per share and sustainable payout ratios. Stock Unlock gives Apple an overall dividend score of about 3.6/5 based on these metrics, suggesting a prudent approach to growing and managing shareholder dividends.",
